1
00:01:21,920 --> 00:01:25,240
Hiring a friend doesn't mean
you can talk down to them

2
00:01:25,320 --> 00:01:26,200
or say whatever.

3
00:01:26,280 --> 00:01:27,920
Bonus, you're being dramatic

4
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:29,360
Fuang hasn't even said anything.

5
00:01:29,440 --> 00:01:31,120
She hasn't, so I have to speak for her.

6
00:01:31,200 --> 00:01:33,080
You can't just stay quiet, can you?

7
00:01:36,600 --> 00:01:37,480
Fuang.

8
00:01:39,280 --> 00:01:40,120
Yes?

9
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:43,200
He seems really determined,
so I'd rather give the spot to him.

10
00:01:47,040 --> 00:01:48,280
Thank you so much.

11
00:01:48,360 --> 00:01:49,520
Hey, you don't have to bow.

12
00:01:49,600 --> 00:01:50,680
That's basically you.

13
00:01:51,480 --> 00:01:53,440
It's cute. I like it.

14
00:01:53,520 --> 00:01:55,440
Even if others don't, I do.

15
00:01:58,080 --> 00:01:59,480
Mee-Bun

16
00:02:00,040 --> 00:02:02,440
might even get you a boyfriend.
Perfect timing.

17
00:02:03,200 --> 00:02:05,160
Don't mess it up, girl!

18
00:02:06,680 --> 00:02:08,479
This is the place.

19
00:02:08,560 --> 00:02:10,479
This is a 14-inch ruler.

20
00:02:11,120 --> 00:02:12,760
-Here.
-Thanks.

21
00:02:12,840 --> 00:02:14,760
This one's 24 inches.

22
00:02:14,840 --> 00:02:16,640
-It's longer.
-Let me see.

23
00:02:17,240 --> 00:02:20,000
And this one's called a curved ruler.

24
00:02:20,080 --> 00:02:21,840
A curved ruler.

25
00:02:38,680 --> 00:02:40,240
-Let's go, Guy.
-Yeah.

26
00:02:40,800 --> 00:02:41,800
-You okay?
-Yeah.

27
00:02:42,640 --> 00:02:45,520
Let's split up here.
I heard you still have work to do.

28
00:02:46,200 --> 00:02:48,280
Thank you so much
for helping me choose all this.

29
00:02:48,360 --> 00:02:51,240
I didn't realize making clothes
required this many tools.

30
00:02:51,320 --> 00:02:54,000
I thought designers just design
and the tailors do the rest.

31
00:02:54,600 --> 00:02:57,800
For clients, yes.
But if you want to run a business,

32
00:02:57,880 --> 00:02:59,160
you have to be well-rounded.

33
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:01,200
-Yes.
-See you.

34
00:03:01,280 --> 00:03:02,160
Bye.

35
00:03:03,320 --> 00:03:04,360
Let's go.

36
00:03:05,240 --> 00:03:06,600
He's that type, right?

37
00:03:07,200 --> 00:03:08,080
What type?

38
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:11,600
I think he likes you.

39
00:03:12,200 --> 00:03:14,800
-Stop it!
-I'm serious! Trust me.

40
00:03:16,160 --> 00:03:19,240
If he liked me,

41
00:03:20,360 --> 00:03:21,480
would you be jealous?

42
00:03:23,600 --> 00:03:25,280
Not jealous. Protective.

43
00:03:27,600 --> 00:03:30,640
You're the only one I have left
to help me with my work.

44
00:03:30,720 --> 00:03:32,960
If you get a boyfriend, I'll lose my help.

45
00:03:33,040 --> 00:03:34,520
So I'm protective.

46
00:03:34,600 --> 00:03:36,320
Don't expect me to let you date easily.

47
00:03:36,400 --> 00:03:37,280
Got it?

48
00:03:39,200 --> 00:03:41,120
Alright, let's go. Your client is waiting.

49
00:04:04,880 --> 00:04:06,160
There you go.

50
00:04:06,240 --> 00:04:07,320
Thank you.

51
00:04:07,400 --> 00:04:10,440
This is my capsule collection, you know.

52
00:04:11,320 --> 00:04:13,200
It's a limited edition collection.

53
00:04:13,280 --> 00:04:16,399
Classic pieces you can wear forever,

54
00:04:16,480 --> 00:04:17,680
beyond trends.

55
00:04:18,720 --> 00:04:21,240
-Yes.
-You seem to know a lot.

56
00:04:21,320 --> 00:04:22,160
Did you study fashion?

57
00:04:22,240 --> 00:04:25,600
Not really. I just like
reading about fashion.

58
00:04:26,680 --> 00:04:30,040
I actually really like your brand.

59
00:04:30,120 --> 00:04:34,000
It's simple, but special in the details.
You can mix and match everything here.

60
00:04:36,040 --> 00:04:39,600
Oh! Actually, we're short-staffed
at the store right now.

61
00:04:39,680 --> 00:04:40,600
Are you interested?

62
00:04:41,600 --> 00:04:44,760
Even if he is, he can't.
He has to go back and help at home.

63
00:04:44,840 --> 00:04:46,640
What does your family do?

64
00:04:46,720 --> 00:04:49,680
My family runs
a ready-to-wear garment factory.

65
00:04:49,760 --> 00:04:50,720
I have to help my uncle.

66
00:04:51,880 --> 00:04:53,080
It's my uncle's business.

67
00:04:54,880 --> 00:04:56,400
That's wonderful.

68
00:04:56,480 --> 00:04:59,120
Then could I have your phone number?

69
00:04:59,200 --> 00:05:03,000
If I want to place orders
with your factory, we can talk.

70
00:05:03,080 --> 00:05:04,440
Sure.

71
00:05:04,520 --> 00:05:05,760
I can also add you on Line.

72
00:05:05,840 --> 00:05:07,480
-Sure.
-Okay.

73
00:05:08,400 --> 00:05:09,680
-Go ahead, scan it.
-Okay.

74
00:05:10,480 --> 00:05:11,920
-Scan it.
-Okay.

75
00:05:12,600 --> 00:05:14,360
Alright. Well then,

76
00:05:14,440 --> 00:05:16,200
you can call or message me anytime.

77
00:05:16,280 --> 00:05:18,440
-I will. I'll text you later.
-Okay.

78
00:05:20,680 --> 00:05:22,160
You're really popular now.

79
00:05:22,240 --> 00:05:24,920
Both men and women are all over you.

80
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:27,800
Being protective of me again?

81
00:05:27,880 --> 00:05:29,320
Not this time.

82
00:05:29,400 --> 00:05:33,080
You're helping me with customer service.
It's a win-win for both of us.

83
00:05:33,160 --> 00:05:34,200
Okay.

84
00:05:41,960 --> 00:05:43,800
Everyone's a content creator these days.

85
00:05:43,880 --> 00:05:46,160
If you're not really famous,
you don't get any views.

86
00:05:46,760 --> 00:05:49,400
I don't even know
what to do for my first episode.

87
00:05:49,480 --> 00:05:51,400
Don't give up yet.

88
00:05:51,480 --> 00:05:53,440
You haven't even tried.

89
00:05:53,520 --> 00:05:55,960
You can do it.
Stop overthinking. Trust me.

90
00:05:56,040 --> 00:05:57,800
Thanks.

91
00:05:59,920 --> 00:06:02,720
Honestly, I kind of want a mentor too.

92
00:06:03,920 --> 00:06:06,080
-I think I--
-Have you seen Cent?

93
00:06:07,360 --> 00:06:09,040
I think I want to ask him for advice.

94
00:06:09,120 --> 00:06:11,600
Maybe he has some good suggestions.

95
00:06:11,680 --> 00:06:13,560
I saw he suggested you study,

96
00:06:13,640 --> 00:06:16,040
and it seems like it worked.
You look really happy now.

97
00:06:16,640 --> 00:06:18,760
Could you help me set up
a meeting with him?

98
00:06:21,080 --> 00:06:24,840
To be honest, I haven't seen him
since the day Pound got drunk.

99
00:06:28,480 --> 00:06:29,720
But Fuang still sees him.

100
00:06:30,320 --> 00:06:31,600
You should ask her.

101
00:06:32,560 --> 00:06:33,920
She's meeting him today.

102
00:06:36,120 --> 00:06:37,040
Today?

103
00:06:37,120 --> 00:06:40,440
Last night, she said she was going
to meet him today to pitch her work.

104
00:06:41,040 --> 00:06:42,600
They should be together right now.

105
00:06:43,760 --> 00:06:45,560
<i>Sorry, I can't.</i>

106
00:06:46,240 --> 00:06:48,120
<i>I already made plans with my mom.</i>

107
00:06:50,640 --> 00:06:51,680
Let's go buy some plants.

108
00:06:51,760 --> 00:06:52,680
Yes?

109
00:06:53,200 --> 00:06:56,840
My mom sent me.
There's a long list. Let's go.

110
00:06:57,480 --> 00:06:59,920
What about the meeting to pitch my work?

111
00:07:00,720 --> 00:07:02,880
We'll just shop
and pitch at the same time.

112
00:07:03,960 --> 00:07:05,080
Okay?

113
00:07:07,240 --> 00:07:08,120
Okay.

114
00:07:10,360 --> 00:07:11,240
Huh?

115
00:07:19,600 --> 00:07:20,760
I'll take everything on this list.

116
00:07:22,640 --> 00:07:25,400
I'll prepare them, but you'll need
to choose the sizes yourself.

117
00:07:26,480 --> 00:07:27,880
Come with me.

118
00:07:29,920 --> 00:07:30,880
If you're ready, start pitching.

119
00:07:33,200 --> 00:07:34,360
Right now?

120
00:07:35,400 --> 00:07:36,240
Are you ready?

121
00:07:38,680 --> 00:07:39,840
I'm ready.

122
00:07:40,720 --> 00:07:41,640
Let's go.

123
00:07:44,200 --> 00:07:47,280
I'm very proud to present this character

124
00:07:47,360 --> 00:07:50,240
because it comes from my own spirit.

125
00:07:50,320 --> 00:07:53,640
Its name is Mee-Bun.
It is a character who has a bun,

126
00:07:53,720 --> 00:07:55,600
which is a hairstyle.

127
00:07:55,680 --> 00:07:59,360
Here. This is what Mee-Bun looks like.

128
00:08:01,960 --> 00:08:05,080
It's someone who loves freedom,
loves the world, loves the environment.

129
00:08:05,880 --> 00:08:08,600
It's determined, has dreams,

130
00:08:08,680 --> 00:08:10,360
but doesn't stick to old rules.

131
00:08:10,440 --> 00:08:11,800
It's a bit quietly rebellious.

132
00:08:12,560 --> 00:08:14,840
It gets happy easily,
but also gets sad easily.

133
00:08:14,920 --> 00:08:16,280
It loves its friends, family--

134
00:08:16,360 --> 00:08:17,560
Excuse me!

135
00:08:17,640 --> 00:08:19,400
What size trees do you want?

136
00:08:27,160 --> 00:08:30,600
I'll take this size and this size.
Same for the rest. Please choose for me.

137
00:08:30,680 --> 00:08:33,200
Sure, I'll arrange it
according to the list.

138
00:08:37,440 --> 00:08:38,559
Cent.

139
00:08:39,280 --> 00:08:41,600
-When Mee-Bun is free, it goes--
-To make merit,

140
00:08:42,760 --> 00:08:44,520
or maybe follow some spiritual beliefs.

141
00:08:47,160 --> 00:08:49,320
How did you know that?

142
00:08:51,440 --> 00:08:52,480
Here.

143
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:54,720
It's right there.

144
00:08:56,200 --> 00:08:57,440
Prayer beads, right?

145
00:09:02,360 --> 00:09:03,600
You noticed it.

146
00:09:04,320 --> 00:09:07,520
That means you were
really paying attention.

147
00:09:08,560 --> 00:09:10,480
So what do you think? Do you like it?

148
00:09:16,320 --> 00:09:18,960
Ma'am, do you have a delivery service?

149
00:09:19,040 --> 00:09:22,640
If you do, load everything into the truck.
Put it all on one bill.

150
00:09:22,720 --> 00:09:23,560
Sure.

151
00:09:25,880 --> 00:09:27,520
Ma'am!

152
00:09:27,600 --> 00:09:30,600
Send someone who can do the landscaping.
I'll pay you extra.

153
00:09:30,680 --> 00:09:31,560
Of course.

154
00:09:33,280 --> 00:09:34,440
It's cute.

155
00:09:37,960 --> 00:09:40,960
Lively, memorable, and has its own style.

156
00:09:42,080 --> 00:09:45,120
You can tell the creator
really put thought into it. It works.

157
00:09:54,400 --> 00:09:56,320
Fuang! Why are you crying?

158
00:09:56,400 --> 00:09:59,280
I never thought this day would come.

159
00:09:59,360 --> 00:10:02,400
Fuang, don't cry anymore. Enough, okay?

160
00:10:14,640 --> 00:10:17,600
Such a crybaby.
You cry when you're happy too.

161
00:10:20,280 --> 00:10:22,840
Praise from someone like you

162
00:10:22,920 --> 00:10:24,520
means a lot to me.

163
00:10:24,600 --> 00:10:28,360
Someone like me? What does that even mean?

164
00:10:28,440 --> 00:10:31,760
A person who's picky,

165
00:10:31,840 --> 00:10:33,760
always finding flaws.

166
00:10:34,680 --> 00:10:36,240
A perfectionist.

167
00:10:39,120 --> 00:10:41,080
If I told my friends

168
00:10:41,160 --> 00:10:43,560
you praised me,

169
00:10:43,640 --> 00:10:45,960
they'd be shocked for sure.

170
00:10:46,760 --> 00:10:48,640
The ones I've met before?

171
00:10:49,240 --> 00:10:50,440
Yeah.

172
00:10:50,520 --> 00:10:52,480
Hey, I'm actually curious.

173
00:10:52,560 --> 00:10:55,160
Why do they want to be business owners?

174
00:10:57,200 --> 00:10:59,360
Probably…

175
00:11:00,240 --> 00:11:01,920
because there's more freedom.

176
00:11:02,520 --> 00:11:05,560
You're your own boss,
not someone's employee.

177
00:11:06,360 --> 00:11:07,320
Oh!

178
00:11:08,160 --> 00:11:12,000
I don't even know what your company does.

179
00:11:13,160 --> 00:11:15,200
We work in technology.

180
00:11:16,080 --> 00:11:17,640
Are you a startup?

181
00:11:17,720 --> 00:11:21,120
We used to be.
We've moved far beyond that.

182
00:11:23,800 --> 00:11:28,240
Do you think being a business owner

183
00:11:28,880 --> 00:11:31,560
is better than being an employee?

184
00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:42,240
No matter what position you're in,

185
00:11:42,320 --> 00:11:43,960
you should think like an owner.

186
00:11:44,920 --> 00:11:47,200
Do the work as if it's your company.

187
00:11:47,800 --> 00:11:51,040
If you have that mindset,
there's no difference.

188
00:11:51,120 --> 00:11:52,880
But as the owner,

189
00:11:52,960 --> 00:11:56,160
you make more money
when the company profits.

190
00:11:56,240 --> 00:11:59,040
But if it fails or loses money,

191
00:11:59,120 --> 00:12:01,080
employees just get laid off.

192
00:12:01,160 --> 00:12:03,560
The owner, though,
is responsible for all the debt.

193
00:12:04,240 --> 00:12:07,840
Everything has two sides,
both pros and cons.

194
00:12:07,920 --> 00:12:11,880
To run a business,
you need to look at people's scars,

195
00:12:12,640 --> 00:12:16,640
not just their success.
Not everyone makes it.

196
00:12:19,520 --> 00:12:20,400
That's true.

197
00:12:25,120 --> 00:12:27,920
When you explain things without scolding,

198
00:12:28,560 --> 00:12:30,120
it's really helpful.

199
00:12:32,440 --> 00:12:36,400
I mean, it makes everything so clear.
It's really good.

200
00:12:48,560 --> 00:12:49,640
Yes, Mom.

201
00:12:49,720 --> 00:12:52,200
Have you finished
buying the plants I asked for?

202
00:12:52,280 --> 00:12:55,920
They're loading them onto the truck.
Once everything's loaded, I'll head back.

203
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:59,320
Don't bring them home.
Send them to Fuang's house instead.

204
00:12:59,400 --> 00:13:02,880
And you take her home too.

205
00:13:03,640 --> 00:13:05,080
How did you know she was here?

206
00:13:05,160 --> 00:13:06,240
I just know.

207
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:09,120
Do what I told you properly.

208
00:13:09,200 --> 00:13:11,280
Next time, if you're going
to ask a girl out,

209
00:13:11,360 --> 00:13:13,280
don't hide it from your mother.

210
00:13:13,360 --> 00:13:17,680
Because I know, I see.
Mother knows best. Okay?

211
00:13:17,760 --> 00:13:19,200
I wasn't asking a girl out.

212
00:13:20,280 --> 00:13:22,920
Hello? Mom?

213
00:13:29,280 --> 00:13:31,120
What did Aunt Eiang say?

214
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:35,720
Hey! The plants are all loaded.
Should we deliver them now?

215
00:13:37,720 --> 00:13:39,440
Yes, go now. Go ahead.

216
00:13:39,520 --> 00:13:41,240
-Alright.
-Okay.

217
00:13:44,240 --> 00:13:47,200
Mom said to send the plants to your house.
Do you want to go home now?

218
00:13:48,440 --> 00:13:50,480
Send the plants to my house?

219
00:13:54,600 --> 00:13:56,720
-All done, sir.
-Thank you.

220
00:14:09,280 --> 00:14:11,760
It's all done now. I'll get going.

221
00:14:11,840 --> 00:14:12,720
-See you.
-Wait!

222
00:14:13,920 --> 00:14:16,040
I wanted to ask about my work.

223
00:14:17,960 --> 00:14:22,160
What should I do next?

224
00:14:22,760 --> 00:14:25,200
It's good. It's cute. It's interesting.

225
00:14:26,480 --> 00:14:28,920
But it's still missing something.
Just a little more.

226
00:14:29,520 --> 00:14:32,520
Some kind of gimmick
that makes people go, "Wow."

227
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:36,000
If you can find that, it'll be perfect.

228
00:14:45,560 --> 00:14:46,680
When I say that,

229
00:14:46,760 --> 00:14:50,160
does it make you
feel pressured, discouraged,

230
00:14:50,680 --> 00:14:51,800
or bad?

231
00:14:54,600 --> 00:14:55,760
No.

232
00:14:56,640 --> 00:14:58,600
The way you said it just now was okay.

233
00:15:00,720 --> 00:15:03,520
Thank you for caring about my feelings.

234
00:15:29,920 --> 00:15:32,080
-Hello.
-Hello.

235
00:15:32,600 --> 00:15:35,000
-Hello.
-Hello.

236
00:15:35,560 --> 00:15:39,240
The plants have been delivered.
I'll be heading back now. Goodbye.

237
00:15:39,320 --> 00:15:40,400
Cent.

238
00:15:40,480 --> 00:15:43,720
I wanted to ask you something.
Is Eiang not feeling well?

239
00:15:45,680 --> 00:15:48,040
I'm not sure. She didn't mention anything.

240
00:15:48,120 --> 00:15:51,360
But I think she seemed unusually tired.

241
00:15:51,440 --> 00:15:53,000
-Your hair. Let me get that for you.
-It's okay, I'll do it.

242
00:15:53,080 --> 00:15:54,360
Oh.

243
00:15:55,040 --> 00:15:57,840
Go wait in the car.
I need to use the bathroom real quick.

244
00:15:59,760 --> 00:16:01,680
Try asking your mom about it, okay?

245
00:16:01,760 --> 00:16:04,360
Thank you very much. I'll head back now.

246
00:16:04,880 --> 00:16:06,920
-Goodbye.
-Take care.

247
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:08,040
Drive safely.

248
00:16:08,120 --> 00:16:09,160
I'm going now.

249
00:16:19,120 --> 00:16:21,320
<i>When will you meet Cent again?</i>

250
00:16:21,400 --> 00:16:25,800
<i>I don't know. We finished the project,</i>
<i>so I don't know when we'll meet again.</i>

251
00:16:36,840 --> 00:16:38,160
CALLING - POUND

252
00:16:43,960 --> 00:16:46,920
Pound, I need your help with something.

253
00:16:51,920 --> 00:16:55,840
Oh, I already had HR submit
the permit application for you.

254
00:16:55,920 --> 00:16:59,600
-Hello.
-You can start whenever you're ready.

255
00:16:59,680 --> 00:17:00,720
Okay.

256
00:17:01,440 --> 00:17:03,040
What do you think? Is it okay?

257
00:17:03,720 --> 00:17:04,599
Yes.

258
00:17:07,040 --> 00:17:08,400
Well, Suea.

259
00:17:09,280 --> 00:17:12,520
Could I work on a flexible basis,
without coming into the office?

260
00:17:13,400 --> 00:17:16,920
I also want to trade in overseas markets.
I want work that isn't desk-bound.

261
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:19,560
It's to avoid burnout.
I don't like staying in my comfort zone.

262
00:17:19,640 --> 00:17:21,000
You think big and you've got guts.

263
00:17:21,960 --> 00:17:25,119
As for how you work, I'm not strict.
It's up to you.

264
00:17:25,200 --> 00:17:27,960
But tonight we're having
an internal celebration party.

265
00:17:28,040 --> 00:17:30,280
-Want to come?
-Yes, I'll go.

266
00:17:33,080 --> 00:17:34,480
-Is it red?
-After you.

267
00:17:34,560 --> 00:17:36,000
Suea!

268
00:17:36,080 --> 00:17:37,560
Drink up!

269
00:17:40,080 --> 00:17:41,720
Wow!

270
00:17:43,120 --> 00:17:44,440
-Keep playing, guys. I'll be right back.
-Yeah.

271
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:48,280
-Here.
-Hey, Suea.

272
00:17:49,360 --> 00:17:51,120
-Wait, this is for me?
-Yeah.

273
00:17:51,200 --> 00:17:52,760
-Whoa.
-Just an appetizer.

274
00:17:52,840 --> 00:17:54,920
-This is crazy.
-There's plenty more inside.

275
00:17:56,720 --> 00:17:59,240
-Red!
-Red!

276
00:18:01,520 --> 00:18:02,560
Drink up.

277
00:18:09,920 --> 00:18:12,040
Bottoms up!

278
00:18:13,960 --> 00:18:15,600
Whoa!

279
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:22,360
Bonus, what are you doing?

280
00:18:22,440 --> 00:18:23,680
Oh.

281
00:18:23,760 --> 00:18:26,520
I'm taking photos
to promote the shop online, Mom.

282
00:18:26,600 --> 00:18:28,880
That way, when we open,
people will already know about it.

283
00:18:28,960 --> 00:18:31,320
-When does the shop open?
-At the beginning of the month.

284
00:18:31,400 --> 00:18:33,360
The mall said the old shop needs to finish

285
00:18:33,440 --> 00:18:35,560
clearing everything out,
then I can move in.

286
00:18:37,840 --> 00:18:40,400
I want to help, but I don't know how.

287
00:18:40,480 --> 00:18:42,520
-I've already told my friends--
-It's okay, Mom.

288
00:18:42,600 --> 00:18:46,200
You're already helping a lot
by not stopping me.

289
00:18:49,280 --> 00:18:51,360
Being a business owner
is tiring, you know.

290
00:18:51,440 --> 00:18:53,640
You have to handle everything on your own.

291
00:18:55,920 --> 00:18:57,560
No problem, Mom.

292
00:18:58,400 --> 00:19:00,960
Oh. Where has Pound gone?

293
00:19:01,560 --> 00:19:05,000
I haven't seen him. If you see him,
tell him to come have dinner.

294
00:19:06,040 --> 00:19:07,640
-Okay.
-Alright.

295
00:19:11,600 --> 00:19:14,280
-Spin it.
-Black!

296
00:19:14,360 --> 00:19:15,520
BONUS

297
00:19:15,600 --> 00:19:18,080
-Black!
-Drink up.

298
00:19:23,960 --> 00:19:26,200
Gold chains, catch!

299
00:19:31,240 --> 00:19:33,360
Whoa, bro!

300
00:19:33,440 --> 00:19:35,360
This is insane!

301
00:19:38,200 --> 00:19:41,640
If you work with me,
we'll have parties like this every month.

302
00:19:41,720 --> 00:19:43,280
Your shirt's coming off.

303
00:19:43,360 --> 00:19:46,000
And if your performance satisfies me,

304
00:19:46,080 --> 00:19:47,920
I'll definitely have a big reward for you.

305
00:19:50,120 --> 00:19:51,400
I like people who dare to take risks.

306
00:19:52,360 --> 00:19:53,840
Are you ready to take that risk with me?

307
00:19:55,760 --> 00:19:56,840
Of course.

308
00:19:56,920 --> 00:19:58,560
That's what I'm talking about!

309
00:19:58,640 --> 00:19:59,600
Let's go!

310
00:20:38,200 --> 00:20:42,000
<i>A gift from my first day at work, Mom.</i>
<i>I'll make lots of money.</i>

311
00:20:42,080 --> 00:20:43,760
<i>You'll be comfortable again.</i>

312
00:21:10,040 --> 00:21:11,800
You want to talk to my dad?

313
00:21:13,080 --> 00:21:14,320
Talk about what?

314
00:21:17,040 --> 00:21:20,680
I'm trading full-time now.
I'm doing it both ways,

315
00:21:20,760 --> 00:21:22,560
trading in the Thai market
for a senior broker

316
00:21:22,640 --> 00:21:24,320
and trading privately in overseas markets.

317
00:21:25,480 --> 00:21:26,320
And?

318
00:21:27,280 --> 00:21:29,480
So I want to talk to your dad.

319
00:21:30,160 --> 00:21:31,760
In case he wants to invest with me.

320
00:21:34,440 --> 00:21:36,040
I barely talk to my dad.

321
00:21:36,760 --> 00:21:40,240
He's still mad
that I didn't work at the factory.

322
00:21:42,080 --> 00:21:44,400
Okay, then. Let's put
my thing aside for now.

323
00:21:44,480 --> 00:21:47,320
Let's talk about you.
What do you want me to help with?

324
00:21:50,040 --> 00:21:52,840
Well, I'm totally stuck.

325
00:21:52,920 --> 00:21:56,200
I still have no idea for episode one,
so I want to ask Cent for advice.

326
00:21:57,920 --> 00:22:00,960
I want to hear more
of his opinion from last time.

327
00:22:01,840 --> 00:22:05,160
But at first, you didn't believe him.
Why did you change your mind now?

328
00:22:05,920 --> 00:22:09,960
Yeah. But Yuan and Fuang listened to him,
and things seemed to work out.

329
00:22:10,960 --> 00:22:13,800
I thought I'd try opening my mind too.
Maybe I'll get some new ideas.

330
00:22:13,880 --> 00:22:16,840
That's why I want your help.
But don't tell Fuang.

331
00:22:17,560 --> 00:22:18,800
Why not?

332
00:22:19,480 --> 00:22:21,960
I made a huge scene with him last time.

333
00:22:22,040 --> 00:22:24,840
I don't want her to know
or make things awkward for her.

334
00:22:28,320 --> 00:22:30,520
Okay. I think I can help.

335
00:22:30,600 --> 00:22:33,280
I guarantee it'll be so smooth.
Fuang won't know a thing. But

336
00:22:33,360 --> 00:22:36,680
if I pull this off,
you have to help me with your dad.

337
00:22:37,760 --> 00:22:38,600
Deal?

338
00:22:42,720 --> 00:22:45,760
And this smooth plan of yours,
how are you going to do it?

339
00:22:54,280 --> 00:22:57,120
This job really means a lot to me, Fuang.

340
00:22:58,920 --> 00:23:02,160
I need to open
as many portfolios as I can.

341
00:23:03,320 --> 00:23:04,840
If I can't do it,

342
00:23:04,920 --> 00:23:07,400
they might kick me off the team.

343
00:23:07,920 --> 00:23:09,080
I'm so stressed.

344
00:23:09,160 --> 00:23:12,600
My family looks down on me,
and work is insanely competitive.

345
00:23:13,440 --> 00:23:16,560
Hey, Pound. Calm down, okay?

346
00:23:17,160 --> 00:23:18,640
Is there anything I can do to help?

347
00:23:18,720 --> 00:23:21,280
If it's investment money, I do have some,

348
00:23:21,360 --> 00:23:23,000
but it's only a few thousand.

349
00:23:23,080 --> 00:23:24,640
Would that help you at all?

350
00:23:24,720 --> 00:23:26,400
I'm not here to take your money.

351
00:23:28,560 --> 00:23:30,440
I don't make money off my friends.

352
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:34,680
But I came to you because…

353
00:23:35,960 --> 00:23:38,640
the person who might be able
to help me right now

354
00:23:39,640 --> 00:23:41,080
is Cent's mom.

355
00:23:43,000 --> 00:23:44,280
You told me before

356
00:23:44,360 --> 00:23:46,800
his mom was going to invest
in your business, right?

357
00:23:46,880 --> 00:23:49,560
And she also invested in Cent's business.

358
00:23:49,640 --> 00:23:51,360
So I thought of her.

359
00:23:52,240 --> 00:23:55,800
You don't have to do much.
Just introduce me, so I can talk to her.

360
00:23:56,800 --> 00:23:58,000
You can come with me too.

361
00:23:58,080 --> 00:24:00,200
I'll explain the investment to her.

362
00:24:00,280 --> 00:24:02,520
Whether she invests or not

363
00:24:03,320 --> 00:24:05,200
is completely up to her.

364
00:24:08,680 --> 00:24:11,960
Please help me, Fuang.

365
00:24:16,880 --> 00:24:17,880
Here.

366
00:24:18,920 --> 00:24:21,360
Your app structure
will look something like this.

367
00:24:22,840 --> 00:24:24,840
-That's awesome!
-Do you understand it?

368
00:24:24,920 --> 00:24:26,080
-Nope.
-Geez.

369
00:24:26,160 --> 00:24:29,480
All that's left is for me
to design the UX and UI, then test it.

370
00:24:29,560 --> 00:24:32,520
Once that's done, we can launch your app.
Then the job's finished.

371
00:24:32,600 --> 00:24:35,880
You'll have to transfer
the shares to me, like we agreed.

372
00:24:35,960 --> 00:24:38,640
Come on, no need to remind me.
I know already!

373
00:24:38,720 --> 00:24:41,160
By the way, do you know
who you'll get to design it?

374
00:24:41,240 --> 00:24:42,680
-I will--
-Oh, Pong!

375
00:24:43,280 --> 00:24:45,360
No. Absolutely not.

376
00:24:45,440 --> 00:24:47,760
You're going to have Pong design it?
No way!

377
00:24:47,840 --> 00:24:49,320
Hey, that's not what I meant.

378
00:24:49,400 --> 00:24:52,160
Pong, call Fuang.
Tell her I have a job for her.

379
00:24:52,240 --> 00:24:54,800
Wait. Hold on.

380
00:24:54,880 --> 00:24:57,320
Easy there, young lady.

381
00:24:57,400 --> 00:25:00,240
Fuang has her own project to work on.
Her pitch nearly passed.

382
00:25:00,320 --> 00:25:02,720
If another job comes up,
she won't finish it.

383
00:25:02,800 --> 00:25:04,280
I want her focused, Mom. No!

384
00:25:04,360 --> 00:25:08,760
She's focused already. She's talented.
Let her do both. She'll make more money.

385
00:25:08,840 --> 00:25:09,960
-Call her!
-Yes.

386
00:25:10,040 --> 00:25:11,240
Stop!

387
00:25:11,320 --> 00:25:13,360
You're set on getting Fuang
to do this job, right?

388
00:25:13,440 --> 00:25:14,640
Yes.

389
00:25:14,720 --> 00:25:17,160
-Even if I say no, you'll still do it.
-Correct.

390
00:25:17,240 --> 00:25:19,520
Okay. If you insist, then…

391
00:25:19,600 --> 00:25:20,920
-I'm calling her now.
-Don't call!

392
00:25:21,000 --> 00:25:22,320
I'll talk to her myself.

393
00:25:30,960 --> 00:25:32,920
If Pong calls,
she won't explain it properly.

394
00:25:33,000 --> 00:25:35,000
-I see.
-I'll handle it myself.

395
00:25:35,080 --> 00:25:38,280
Okay.

396
00:25:38,360 --> 00:25:39,600
Whoa.

397
00:25:50,280 --> 00:25:53,600
I'M HERE. CAN YOU MAKE IT TO CLASS TODAY?

398
00:26:10,040 --> 00:26:12,200
-Yuan, are you done?
-Yes, all done.

399
00:26:12,280 --> 00:26:13,120
Okay.

400
00:26:22,160 --> 00:26:23,000
Where are you going?

401
00:26:23,080 --> 00:26:26,000
I have a meeting with a client.
We're going over some more details.

402
00:26:26,080 --> 00:26:28,040
After you talk to the client,
update me too.

403
00:26:28,120 --> 00:26:29,440
Sure. See you.

404
00:26:37,200 --> 00:26:39,480
I'm here. Sorry. I just…

405
00:26:40,680 --> 00:26:42,680
You left it the other day,
so I kept it for you.

406
00:26:44,800 --> 00:26:46,480
Thank you so much.

407
00:26:46,560 --> 00:26:48,800
Sorry for looking through it
without asking.

408
00:26:48,880 --> 00:26:50,120
It's okay.

409
00:26:50,200 --> 00:26:52,320
I just draw random stuff.

410
00:26:52,400 --> 00:26:54,800
Whenever something comes to mind,
I sketch it out.

411
00:26:54,880 --> 00:26:57,280
If you add a bit of street style to it,

412
00:26:57,360 --> 00:26:58,280
it'll really hit.

413
00:26:58,360 --> 00:27:00,480
And your designs are so detailed,

414
00:27:00,560 --> 00:27:03,040
-I can pattern them and get them produced.
-Really?

415
00:27:03,640 --> 00:27:07,080
Actually, I do want to do it.

416
00:27:07,160 --> 00:27:10,600
But there's just one problem.

417
00:27:10,680 --> 00:27:12,160
I don't have the funds.

418
00:27:12,240 --> 00:27:14,160
If it's about money, I can help.

419
00:27:14,760 --> 00:27:17,880
Honestly, I've wanted to start
my own clothing brand for a long time.

420
00:27:17,960 --> 00:27:21,200
I have everything ready.
I'm just missing great ideas like these.

421
00:27:21,280 --> 00:27:23,240
If you're okay with it,
why don't we go for it?

422
00:27:25,200 --> 00:27:26,040
You'd really fund me?

423
00:27:32,480 --> 00:27:34,280
I don't want to take advantage of you.

424
00:27:34,920 --> 00:27:37,320
I don't know anything about business.

425
00:27:39,160 --> 00:27:42,320
What if we do it and it fails?

426
00:27:42,960 --> 00:27:44,480
I'm afraid you'll lose money for nothing.

427
00:27:45,320 --> 00:27:46,160
Yuan.

428
00:27:47,400 --> 00:27:50,560
With skills and passion like yours,

429
00:27:51,240 --> 00:27:52,800
if you get a chance, just go for it.

430
00:27:54,080 --> 00:27:56,480
As for the business side, don't worry.
I'll help with that.

431
00:27:57,000 --> 00:27:59,400
We can start small.
We don't have to make too many pieces.

432
00:27:59,480 --> 00:28:00,960
Think of it as testing the market.

433
00:28:01,040 --> 00:28:03,560
Once customers find us,
we can slowly expand.

434
00:28:05,360 --> 00:28:08,120
Okay. If you're ready to go for it,

435
00:28:08,800 --> 00:28:10,240
then I'm ready too.

436
00:28:11,280 --> 00:28:13,200
I'll bring the ideas and do the work.

437
00:28:13,920 --> 00:28:17,000
As for the money,
I'll have to rely on you for all of it.

438
00:28:17,080 --> 00:28:18,160
Deal!

439
00:28:19,800 --> 00:28:21,080
Deal!

440
00:28:21,160 --> 00:28:24,120
-Thank you so much, Guy.
-You don't have to thank me that much.

441
00:28:26,360 --> 00:28:27,400
What's your brand called?

442
00:28:27,480 --> 00:28:29,520
My brand is called Gaya.

443
00:28:29,600 --> 00:28:32,880
The letters are G-A-Y-A.

444
00:28:32,960 --> 00:28:35,920
I combined my name with Guy's name.

445
00:28:37,400 --> 00:28:38,680
Can you help me design the logo?

446
00:28:38,760 --> 00:28:40,840
Sure. No problem. Hold on.

447
00:28:41,520 --> 00:28:42,480
Let me write down your brand's name.

448
00:28:44,120 --> 00:28:47,600
-G-A-Y-A.
-Yeah.

449
00:28:48,680 --> 00:28:50,040
Thanks.

450
00:28:50,120 --> 00:28:53,640
I'm happy for you.
Finally, your dream is coming true.

451
00:28:54,320 --> 00:28:56,600
Honestly, it's like

452
00:28:56,680 --> 00:28:58,440
a dream come true by total luck.

453
00:28:58,520 --> 00:29:01,120
I'm still confused.
Like, is this really happening?

454
00:29:02,760 --> 00:29:06,440
Same. When Aunt Eiang funded me,
it felt just like this. Totally surreal.

455
00:29:06,520 --> 00:29:08,400
Really? You felt this confused too?

456
00:29:08,480 --> 00:29:09,880
Yeah, I was so confused back then.

457
00:29:11,200 --> 00:29:13,760
Hey, you're getting to follow your dream.

458
00:29:13,840 --> 00:29:16,240
Bonus's shop is coming together too.

459
00:29:16,320 --> 00:29:17,520
Oh.

460
00:29:17,600 --> 00:29:20,560
Has Pound talked to you about work?

461
00:29:20,640 --> 00:29:22,240
-No, he hasn't.
-Really?

462
00:29:24,080 --> 00:29:25,600
He came to me.

463
00:29:26,560 --> 00:29:29,800
He said he wants me to take him
to talk to Cent's mom.

464
00:29:31,560 --> 00:29:33,480
He wants to ask her to invest.

465
00:29:37,720 --> 00:29:41,440
I do want to help him.
He looked really stressed.

466
00:29:43,160 --> 00:29:47,400
But I don't know how to start talking
to Aunt Eiang about it.

467
00:29:54,400 --> 00:29:56,800
Fuang, I have work to discuss with you.

468
00:29:59,400 --> 00:30:00,400
Privately.

469
00:30:01,600 --> 00:30:02,480
Okay.

470
00:30:07,960 --> 00:30:09,120
"Privately."

471
00:30:18,720 --> 00:30:22,640
Do you know why the order button

472
00:30:23,160 --> 00:30:26,680
is at the bottom when we shop online?

473
00:30:28,080 --> 00:30:30,920
Because that's where the thumb reaches.

474
00:30:31,000 --> 00:30:34,120
Then why are most order buttons blue?

475
00:30:34,200 --> 00:30:38,440
Blue is the color of trust and comfort.

476
00:30:39,280 --> 00:30:42,920
When customers see it,
they feel at ease about placing an order.

477
00:30:43,000 --> 00:30:44,760
If you want people

478
00:30:44,840 --> 00:30:47,160
to decide to buy faster,
what should you do?

479
00:30:47,240 --> 00:30:48,720
Don't give them too many choices.

480
00:30:48,800 --> 00:30:51,720
The more choices there are,
the slower they decide.

481
00:30:51,800 --> 00:30:54,280
If customers can't decide,
they might not buy at all.

482
00:30:54,360 --> 00:30:55,920
As for what you want to sell,

483
00:30:56,000 --> 00:30:58,760
put it in the first or last image.

484
00:30:58,840 --> 00:31:00,400
Because most people

485
00:31:00,480 --> 00:31:02,920
remember those better
than the images in the middle.

486
00:31:03,480 --> 00:31:04,720
Why are you asking, Cent?

487
00:31:06,320 --> 00:31:09,520
Nothing. I just wanted to know
if you studied it.

488
00:31:09,600 --> 00:31:10,880
Of course I did.

489
00:31:10,960 --> 00:31:13,920
I took UX and UI as an elective.

490
00:31:14,000 --> 00:31:14,920
And I got an A too.

491
00:31:17,000 --> 00:31:18,880
Very good. You can start
working right away.

492
00:31:18,960 --> 00:31:20,080
Huh?

493
00:31:20,160 --> 00:31:21,240
Let's sit.

494
00:31:22,480 --> 00:31:25,200
Start working? What work?

495
00:31:25,280 --> 00:31:27,080
I'm completely confused right now.

496
00:31:30,320 --> 00:31:31,480
Yuan.

497
00:31:32,080 --> 00:31:34,280
-What are you watching?
-Dad, Mom, hide!

498
00:31:34,360 --> 00:31:35,200
Quick, hide.

499
00:31:39,080 --> 00:31:40,080
Oh.

500
00:31:40,160 --> 00:31:41,120
Right now,

501
00:31:41,200 --> 00:31:44,320
I have to design
the UX and UI for an application.

502
00:31:44,400 --> 00:31:47,320
My mom wants you to do it. Interested?

503
00:31:47,960 --> 00:31:48,920
I am.

504
00:31:50,840 --> 00:31:52,160
But…

505
00:31:54,640 --> 00:31:55,760
Can I ask

506
00:31:56,360 --> 00:31:59,720
for something in exchange?

507
00:32:00,840 --> 00:32:01,920
Go ahead.

508
00:32:02,000 --> 00:32:03,280
Right now,

509
00:32:03,360 --> 00:32:06,480
Pound is starting a new job.

510
00:32:06,560 --> 00:32:09,400
He's an investment advisor, Cent.

511
00:32:09,480 --> 00:32:12,760
He wants to talk to Aunt Eiang.

512
00:32:12,840 --> 00:32:15,360
Can I take him to meet her?

513
00:32:15,440 --> 00:32:16,880
If you're okay with that,

514
00:32:16,960 --> 00:32:19,560
I'll take this job.
I can start right away.

515
00:32:19,640 --> 00:32:21,760
Do you realize
how much you love your friends?

516
00:32:22,520 --> 00:32:24,800
You've negotiated for a friend twice now.

517
00:32:24,880 --> 00:32:27,120
But this time,
Pound really is in a tough spot.

518
00:32:29,360 --> 00:32:31,640
If there's anything I can do to help,
I want to help.

519
00:32:31,720 --> 00:32:33,040
Alright.

520
00:32:33,720 --> 00:32:36,760
I'll ask my mother for you, then. But

521
00:32:37,520 --> 00:32:40,040
it's up to her whether she agrees or not.

522
00:32:41,640 --> 00:32:42,600
Okay.

523
00:32:42,680 --> 00:32:43,960
Set it up, then.

524
00:32:44,040 --> 00:32:44,920
Okay.

525
00:32:45,960 --> 00:32:48,240
But you're sure he's just a friend,

526
00:32:48,320 --> 00:32:50,120
not a boyfriend, right?

527
00:32:56,360 --> 00:32:58,280
Is he handsome, Mr. Cent?

528
00:33:02,000 --> 00:33:04,040
Well, he's not bad-looking.

529
00:33:05,880 --> 00:33:09,280
Caring for each other like this,
he might be more than just a friend.

530
00:33:09,360 --> 00:33:10,640
True!

531
00:33:12,320 --> 00:33:14,880
When he comes to talk to you,
I'm coming to listen too.

532
00:33:14,960 --> 00:33:16,760
I want to know what he's selling.

533
00:33:18,640 --> 00:33:21,920
It's because you're like this, Mom.
You keep giving money to people.

534
00:33:22,000 --> 00:33:23,320
You'll go soft again.

535
00:33:31,560 --> 00:33:33,120
Really, Fuang?

536
00:33:35,240 --> 00:33:36,840
Thank you so much.

537
00:33:36,920 --> 00:33:38,720
Whenever his mom is free

538
00:33:38,800 --> 00:33:42,040
and I can go talk to her,
just let me know. I'm more than ready.

539
00:33:42,560 --> 00:33:44,160
Thank you so much.

540
00:33:45,200 --> 00:33:46,920
Yeah, see you later.

541
00:33:52,440 --> 00:33:53,640
PEOPLE I KNOW

542
00:33:53,720 --> 00:33:54,960
AUNT EIANG, CENT'S MOM

543
00:34:01,560 --> 00:34:04,320
Mom said you got a job. What kind of job?

544
00:34:04,400 --> 00:34:06,200
Why are they giving out gold
on your first day?

545
00:34:06,280 --> 00:34:08,199
Let's not talk about that yet.

546
00:34:08,280 --> 00:34:11,400
I actually wanted to talk to you
about something. These days,

547
00:34:11,480 --> 00:34:13,600
-how much do you make a month?
-Why are you asking?

548
00:34:13,679 --> 00:34:16,000
Hey, I'm asking because I care.

549
00:34:16,080 --> 00:34:17,880
I want to help you make money
without working so hard.

550
00:34:17,960 --> 00:34:20,239
Spend money to make money.
Let your money work for you.

551
00:34:20,320 --> 00:34:23,639
If you want to get rich fast,
I can help you find a way

552
00:34:23,719 --> 00:34:26,120
to grow your money on its own. Interested?

553
00:34:26,199 --> 00:34:27,120
Nonsense!

554
00:34:28,400 --> 00:34:30,639
There's no such thing
as getting rich without working.

555
00:34:31,719 --> 00:34:34,760
Methods like that
are made to fool greedy people.

556
00:34:34,840 --> 00:34:35,719
Dad!

557
00:34:36,360 --> 00:34:39,520
If you don't agree,
can you not get in my way?

558
00:34:39,600 --> 00:34:41,000
I'm not getting in your way.

559
00:34:41,080 --> 00:34:42,800
I'm just trying
to knock some sense into you.

560
00:34:42,880 --> 00:34:45,239
Seeing you set up
your computers like this, I already know.

561
00:34:45,320 --> 00:34:49,360
Plenty of my friends got into stocks
and lost everything.

562
00:34:49,440 --> 00:34:51,040
But I'm not your friends, Dad.

563
00:34:51,920 --> 00:34:54,600
Don't judge me by them
and assume I'll fail like they did.

564
00:34:54,679 --> 00:34:56,000
And more importantly,

565
00:34:56,560 --> 00:34:58,280
I won't fail like you either.

566
00:34:58,800 --> 00:35:00,560
-Pound!
-Dad, don't.

567
00:35:01,560 --> 00:35:02,440
Calm down.

568
00:35:02,520 --> 00:35:03,880
You think you're so smart, huh?

569
00:35:04,600 --> 00:35:06,400
They gave you a little gold,

570
00:35:06,480 --> 00:35:09,480
and now you think
you're better than everyone else?

571
00:35:12,040 --> 00:35:13,920
I don't think I'm better than anyone, Dad.

572
00:35:14,960 --> 00:35:16,640
I just don't understand

573
00:35:16,720 --> 00:35:20,280
why you always have to tear me down
and put pressure on me.

574
00:35:21,600 --> 00:35:23,480
Like you don't want me
to do better than you.

575
00:35:23,560 --> 00:35:25,440
Pound, enough.

576
00:35:25,520 --> 00:35:27,680
Dad said that
because he's worried about you.

577
00:35:27,760 --> 00:35:29,240
Worried?

578
00:35:29,320 --> 00:35:31,800
He's clearly scolding me.
He's never worried about me.

579
00:35:31,880 --> 00:35:33,800
If you don't stop
being this full of yourself,

580
00:35:34,400 --> 00:35:37,240
with these stupid fantasies,
I'll scold you like this every day.

581
00:35:37,320 --> 00:35:38,600
See, Pung? He admitted it.

582
00:35:38,680 --> 00:35:40,760
He's scolding me.
He's not worried about me at all.

583
00:35:40,840 --> 00:35:42,360
Anything else you want to scold me for?

584
00:35:42,440 --> 00:35:44,240
-Dad!
-What's going on here?

585
00:35:44,320 --> 00:35:45,920
Enough. Stop it.

586
00:35:47,520 --> 00:35:49,320
Pung, take your dad out first.

587
00:35:49,920 --> 00:35:51,600
-Yes.
-Go outside for now.

588
00:35:51,680 --> 00:35:53,760
-Come on, Dad.
-If it were that easy to get rich,

589
00:35:54,360 --> 00:35:57,080
everyone would be rich by now.
Remember what I said.

590
00:35:57,160 --> 00:36:00,200
The stock market is not a playground.
Remember that!

591
00:36:00,280 --> 00:36:01,760
-Let's go, Dad.
-Take him outside.

592
00:36:02,480 --> 00:36:03,320
Come on, Dad.

593
00:36:09,600 --> 00:36:13,480
Pound, I really appreciate the gold.

594
00:36:13,560 --> 00:36:15,960
But if the work
you're doing is risky, I don't--

595
00:36:16,040 --> 00:36:17,160
Mom, don't listen to Dad.

596
00:36:17,960 --> 00:36:20,240
People trade stocks all over the world.

597
00:36:20,320 --> 00:36:21,720
It's not that scary.

598
00:36:21,800 --> 00:36:24,280
These days, everyone downloads an app
and trades by themselves.

599
00:36:24,360 --> 00:36:26,360
If we're talking about risk,

600
00:36:26,960 --> 00:36:29,360
aren't all kinds of investment risky?

601
00:36:29,440 --> 00:36:31,800
I studied this. I got my license properly.

602
00:36:33,120 --> 00:36:34,920
Please believe me, Mom.

603
00:36:36,400 --> 00:36:38,880
I'll make our family rich again.

604
00:36:39,600 --> 00:36:41,280
Please believe me, Mom

605
00:36:46,320 --> 00:36:48,280
I believe you can do it.

606
00:36:48,360 --> 00:36:52,160
Don't give up. I understand how you feel.

607
00:36:52,240 --> 00:36:56,480
I just don't understand why dads
are so good at destroying dreams.

608
00:36:57,000 --> 00:36:59,440
<i>Maybe they live too much in reality.</i>

609
00:36:59,520 --> 00:37:02,680
So much that they forget
a lot of realities were once dreams too.

610
00:37:03,560 --> 00:37:04,760
That's deep!

611
00:37:04,840 --> 00:37:07,440
I'm trying to understand my own dad too.

612
00:37:07,520 --> 00:37:09,400
I don't want to let it stress me out.

613
00:37:10,200 --> 00:37:12,080
I'm trying to turn it into energy instead.

614
00:37:12,160 --> 00:37:14,160
I want him to see that I can do it.

615
00:37:14,240 --> 00:37:15,760
That's how I think too.

616
00:37:15,840 --> 00:37:18,960
The more my dad looks down on me,
the more I want to prove I can do it.

617
00:37:19,040 --> 00:37:22,480
I believe that in every crisis,
there has to be an opportunity.

618
00:37:22,560 --> 00:37:25,800
We just have to be brave enough to seize
that opportunity and make it ours.

619
00:37:26,800 --> 00:37:29,480
Talking to you makes me feel hopeful.

620
00:37:29,560 --> 00:37:30,600
<i>Bonus.</i>

621
00:37:30,680 --> 00:37:32,600
Thanks so much for worrying about me.

622
00:37:34,120 --> 00:37:35,480
I feel better now.

623
00:37:36,320 --> 00:37:38,720
Oh! On your shop's opening day,
I'll come help out.

624
00:37:38,800 --> 00:37:41,240
You believe I can open my shop,

625
00:37:41,320 --> 00:37:43,960
so I believe you can get rich too.

626
00:37:45,000 --> 00:37:46,200
We'll get rich together.

627
00:37:47,000 --> 00:37:48,400
-Good night.
-<i>Good night.</i>

628
00:37:50,720 --> 00:37:53,040
I didn't want to transfer the logo fee.

629
00:37:53,760 --> 00:37:55,040
I wanted to give it to you in person.

630
00:37:55,120 --> 00:37:57,680
I told you already, I don't want it.
I did it for free.

631
00:37:57,760 --> 00:37:59,280
I don't want to feel like I owe you.

632
00:38:00,720 --> 00:38:03,520
I don't want to use our friendship
as an excuse to take advantage of you.

633
00:38:04,160 --> 00:38:07,560
Take advantage? I don't think
you're taking advantage of me.

634
00:38:08,840 --> 00:38:10,520
Friends are supposed to help each other.

635
00:38:10,600 --> 00:38:11,840
Help?

636
00:38:13,440 --> 00:38:16,360
I think we're adults now.
If we're working seriously,

637
00:38:17,160 --> 00:38:19,160
then we should just treat it as work.

638
00:38:19,720 --> 00:38:23,120
Keep things clear.
Nothing behind each other's backs.

639
00:38:26,440 --> 00:38:27,520
Behind each other's backs?

640
00:38:31,120 --> 00:38:33,960
I don't get it.
What are you trying to say?

641
00:38:34,040 --> 00:38:37,760
You say this is clear,
but it sounds unclear to me.

642
00:38:38,840 --> 00:38:42,360
Let's just say I want to pay you.
I don't want to feel like I owe anyone.

643
00:38:43,280 --> 00:38:44,960
And I want to grow on my own.

644
00:38:45,600 --> 00:38:46,920
I don't want to rely on anyone anymore.

645
00:38:47,600 --> 00:38:50,840
Being on your own
and succeeding on your own is best.

646
00:38:50,920 --> 00:38:53,160
Because the people
who used to help us all the time

647
00:38:54,000 --> 00:38:55,360
might not want to help us anymore.

648
00:38:56,800 --> 00:38:58,040
Just take the money.

649
00:38:58,760 --> 00:38:59,800
I can earn it in no time.

650
00:39:11,160 --> 00:39:13,000
Franc is right, dear.

651
00:39:13,080 --> 00:39:17,280
If you don't overthink it,
maybe that really is all she meant.

652
00:39:21,040 --> 00:39:22,400
Then,

653
00:39:23,080 --> 00:39:25,920
have you ever fought
with a friend over profit?

654
00:39:26,000 --> 00:39:29,000
I haven't, but your dad has many times.

655
00:39:29,080 --> 00:39:31,760
Your dad's been ripped off by friends
more times than I can count.

656
00:39:35,080 --> 00:39:37,480
Oh, and how are your friends doing?

657
00:39:37,560 --> 00:39:40,160
I used to see you all having parties
at Bonus's house a lot.

658
00:39:40,240 --> 00:39:41,920
Do you still see each other these days?

659
00:39:42,840 --> 00:39:46,120
Not really. Everyone's busy.

660
00:39:46,200 --> 00:39:48,680
The one I see most often is Yuan.

661
00:39:48,760 --> 00:39:51,520
But lately, he's been making clothes
with his senior,

662
00:39:51,600 --> 00:39:52,680
so I haven't seen him either.

663
00:39:52,760 --> 00:39:54,320
This is it.

664
00:39:54,400 --> 00:39:56,760
This is what adult life is.

665
00:39:56,840 --> 00:39:58,920
We have to take responsibility
for our own lives.

666
00:39:59,000 --> 00:40:02,280
We each have our own path.
Sometimes, it's hard

667
00:40:02,360 --> 00:40:05,240
to separate benefits from friendship.

668
00:40:10,520 --> 00:40:11,920
Take it.

669
00:40:16,960 --> 00:40:20,360
Remember this, Fuang. The best you can do

670
00:40:20,440 --> 00:40:23,480
is make sure profit
doesn't ruin your friendship.

671
00:40:25,320 --> 00:40:27,400
Have you passed
the investment consultant exam?

672
00:40:27,480 --> 00:40:30,520
Yes, I've passed
both IC Plain and IC Complex.

673
00:40:30,600 --> 00:40:32,920
I've got the IC Complex One license.

674
00:40:33,000 --> 00:40:35,160
I can recommend all market products

675
00:40:35,240 --> 00:40:37,080
and handle futures contracts.

676
00:40:37,160 --> 00:40:39,560
And right now,
I'm about to take the IP exam,

677
00:40:39,640 --> 00:40:42,840
so I'll be able to fully manage
individual portfolios.

678
00:40:47,000 --> 00:40:48,080
How many years have you been working?

679
00:40:48,160 --> 00:40:50,080
I only started working recently,

680
00:40:50,160 --> 00:40:52,160
but I've been trading stocks
since high school.

681
00:40:52,240 --> 00:40:54,720
So it's been almost ten years now.

682
00:40:54,800 --> 00:40:56,480
Back then, there weren't any apps.

683
00:40:56,560 --> 00:40:59,560
You had to trade through a broker only,
which was pretty slow.

684
00:40:59,640 --> 00:41:00,960
If it's fast, it's easy to mess up.

685
00:41:01,040 --> 00:41:04,560
I think if someone's going to mess up,
they'll do it either way.

686
00:41:07,120 --> 00:41:10,920
I'm here because I don't want you
to miss this investment opportunity.

687
00:41:11,000 --> 00:41:12,000
Really?

688
00:41:12,960 --> 00:41:15,680
What kind of investment
are you interested in?

689
00:41:15,760 --> 00:41:19,080
Fast and exciting or slow but sure?

690
00:41:19,160 --> 00:41:21,840
-Let me ask you directly.
-Sure.

691
00:41:21,920 --> 00:41:23,840
Do you like buying lottery tickets?

692
00:41:23,920 --> 00:41:25,360
Often, dear.

693
00:41:27,400 --> 00:41:28,400
Are you here to recommend investments

694
00:41:29,560 --> 00:41:30,760
or sell a pyramid scheme?

695
00:41:34,120 --> 00:41:35,120
Cent!

696
00:41:35,640 --> 00:41:37,120
Why would you talk to him like that?

697
00:41:40,040 --> 00:41:42,680
It's okay, Auntie. I understand Cent.

698
00:41:42,760 --> 00:41:45,880
Usually, consultants don't hard-sell
as much as I do.

699
00:41:46,480 --> 00:41:50,200
But since we know each other,
I'm just keeping the pitch casual.

700
00:41:50,280 --> 00:41:53,920
That's not called being professional.
Investing needs principles and formality.

701
00:41:54,000 --> 00:41:55,600
Not knocking on someone's door
like direct sales.

702
00:41:55,680 --> 00:41:57,640
That doesn't look trustworthy.

703
00:41:57,720 --> 00:41:59,640
Are you trying to scam money
out of an old lady?

704
00:41:59,720 --> 00:42:02,680
Hey! I'm not old yet.

705
00:42:03,440 --> 00:42:05,240
Here, son. Eat up.

706
00:42:05,320 --> 00:42:07,720
-Mom!
-That’ll keep your mouth busy.

707
00:42:08,840 --> 00:42:09,840
You talk too much.

708
00:42:11,200 --> 00:42:13,560
How about this?
Let me give you some basic advice.

709
00:42:13,640 --> 00:42:17,160
Whether you're interested or not,
we can decide again later.

710
00:42:17,240 --> 00:42:18,560
Okay.

711
00:42:18,640 --> 00:42:20,480
There are many types of investments,

712
00:42:20,560 --> 00:42:23,840
but the one I'm good at,
and the one I think brings fast profits,

713
00:42:23,920 --> 00:42:25,320
is investing in the stock market.

714
00:42:25,400 --> 00:42:28,120
Fast profits. Instant bankruptcy.

715
00:42:30,280 --> 00:42:32,520
-You really have a foul mouth.
-That hurts.

716
00:42:32,600 --> 00:42:36,520
There are many stock markets.
In Thailand, it's regulated by the SEC.

717
00:42:37,120 --> 00:42:40,440
But for overseas markets,
I recommend currency trading.

718
00:42:40,520 --> 00:42:43,200
The risk is high,
but the profits are high too.

719
00:42:43,280 --> 00:42:44,720
But it's still not SEC-certified.

720
00:42:44,800 --> 00:42:46,640
Many people invested
and got their money stuck overseas.

721
00:42:47,240 --> 00:42:48,760
They couldn't bring it back.

722
00:42:49,920 --> 00:42:52,120
Don't mind him, dear. Go on.

723
00:42:52,200 --> 00:42:54,320
If I want to do currency trading,
what do I have to do?

724
00:42:54,400 --> 00:42:55,920
You can apply online right away.

725
00:42:56,000 --> 00:42:59,160
You only need your ID card
and bankbook to verify your identity.

726
00:42:59,240 --> 00:43:01,600
And don't worry about money getting stuck.

727
00:43:01,680 --> 00:43:04,480
If you want to close the account or stop,
I'll take care of it for you.

728
00:43:04,560 --> 00:43:06,560
-Mom, if you don't understand--
-Stop! Be quiet!

729
00:43:07,920 --> 00:43:09,680
I'm investing one million.

730
00:43:10,640 --> 00:43:12,160
And if you don't stop talking,

731
00:43:12,240 --> 00:43:13,920
it'll become two million.

732
00:43:14,680 --> 00:43:15,800
Mom!

733
00:43:15,880 --> 00:43:18,760
If you knew even a little about investing,
I wouldn't say anything,

734
00:43:18,840 --> 00:43:21,000
-but you don't know anything about this.
-Two million!

735
00:43:21,960 --> 00:43:25,600
If you don't stop talking,
it'll be three. Three million.

736
00:43:31,520 --> 00:43:34,440
Send me the username and password too,
so I can sign in and check.

737
00:43:35,040 --> 00:43:36,480
If the chart drags the portfolio
close to blowing up,

738
00:43:36,560 --> 00:43:39,440
I can average down or close the order
before the losses get ugly.

739
00:43:40,440 --> 00:43:42,600
Or if it goes the wrong way
and can't be saved,

740
00:43:43,120 --> 00:43:45,480
I can take the money out
without telling her. Don't scold me.

741
00:43:45,560 --> 00:43:47,480
I'm doing this to protect you.

742
00:43:51,400 --> 00:43:55,000
I'm going to talk to Cent
about work for a bit.

743
00:44:00,480 --> 00:44:02,440
Then shall we start opening the account?

744
00:44:02,520 --> 00:44:03,960
-Sure.
-Okay.

745
00:44:05,200 --> 00:44:06,920
You can fill out the application here.

746
00:44:10,600 --> 00:44:12,840
Cent.

747
00:44:15,560 --> 00:44:17,520
Earlier,

748
00:44:18,360 --> 00:44:21,560
if Pound made you uncomfortable,
I'm sorry.

749
00:44:22,280 --> 00:44:23,560
Please don't be mad at him.

750
00:44:25,320 --> 00:44:27,440
I'm not mad. I'm worried.

751
00:44:28,680 --> 00:44:30,160
Worried about Pound?

752
00:44:31,320 --> 00:44:34,560
Why would I worry about him?
He's slick enough to handle himself.

753
00:44:35,080 --> 00:44:36,200
I'm worried about you.

754
00:44:37,440 --> 00:44:41,000
Besides my mom,
did you introduce anyone else?

755
00:44:41,080 --> 00:44:42,320
No.

756
00:44:42,400 --> 00:44:45,800
Good. Don't get too involved. Understand?

757
00:44:46,400 --> 00:44:48,800
Cent, you're worried about me?

758
00:44:52,360 --> 00:44:53,280
Yeah.

759
00:44:56,360 --> 00:44:57,480
Thank you.

760
00:44:58,920 --> 00:45:02,200
I held up my end. You got what you wanted.
Now don't forget the work.

761
00:45:02,280 --> 00:45:03,200
Come get the brief soon.

762
00:45:03,280 --> 00:45:04,720
Yes, sir!

763
00:45:06,800 --> 00:45:07,800
What's wrong with you?

764
00:45:15,320 --> 00:45:16,160
Whoa.

765
00:45:16,240 --> 00:45:18,280
Do I have to trade all of this, Pound?

766
00:45:18,360 --> 00:45:21,080
No. We'll start
by trading in just two markets.

767
00:45:21,160 --> 00:45:23,000
I recommend the US market.

768
00:45:23,080 --> 00:45:24,240
Okay.

769
00:45:24,320 --> 00:45:26,400
Whatever you say.
You're the one trading, after all.

770
00:45:26,480 --> 00:45:30,720
Yes. Once we profit, the money
goes into the broker's account overseas.

771
00:45:30,800 --> 00:45:33,360
Then you just transfer it back
into your Thai account.

772
00:45:33,440 --> 00:45:36,600
As for the profit, we'll split it 50-50.

773
00:45:37,200 --> 00:45:38,200
Is that okay with you?

774
00:45:38,280 --> 00:45:41,760
Of course. No problem.
I just want to help Fuang's friend.

775
00:45:42,360 --> 00:45:44,280
-Thank you so much, Auntie.
-Yes.

776
00:45:47,520 --> 00:45:51,240
Auntie, Cent knows a lot
about investing too.

777
00:45:51,320 --> 00:45:52,840
He even knows
about the username and password.

778
00:45:52,920 --> 00:45:55,920
That kind of thing is right up his alley.
It's basically his job.

779
00:45:58,920 --> 00:46:01,120
May I ask what he does for work?

780
00:46:05,000 --> 00:46:06,120
Pay-Wai?

781
00:46:07,520 --> 00:46:09,320
They write programs and design systems

782
00:46:09,400 --> 00:46:11,840
to make online payments
as easy and fast as possible.

783
00:46:11,920 --> 00:46:14,560
They have two branches
in Japan and Singapore.

784
00:46:14,640 --> 00:46:17,280
He's the founder
and a partner in the company.

785
00:46:17,360 --> 00:46:18,800
He owns it?

786
00:46:18,880 --> 00:46:21,160
When Aunt Eiang told me up to that point,

787
00:46:21,240 --> 00:46:22,720
I immediately thought of Peace.

788
00:46:23,320 --> 00:46:25,640
I remembered he once told me
that a Thai guy

789
00:46:25,720 --> 00:46:27,880
had started a payment gateway
with a Japanese friend.

790
00:46:27,960 --> 00:46:31,880
The guy's super famous and rich.
But I never imagined it would be Cent.

791
00:46:31,960 --> 00:46:33,840
Because he has all kinds of clients,

792
00:46:33,920 --> 00:46:37,080
he knows enough to take you guys down,
just like on the first day you met.

793
00:46:39,720 --> 00:46:41,360
This is all the information
I have for now.

794
00:46:41,440 --> 00:46:44,480
But I still can't think of a way
to get you to talk to him.

795
00:46:45,640 --> 00:46:49,120
But I think you should tell Fuang.

796
00:46:49,200 --> 00:46:51,000
If she knows, she'll definitely help you.

797
00:46:51,720 --> 00:46:53,560
Not necessarily.

798
00:46:53,640 --> 00:46:57,560
She's willing to help you.
She might not be willing to help me.

799
00:46:59,320 --> 00:47:01,360
I don't want to bother her.

800
00:47:01,440 --> 00:47:03,400
If you figure out a way,
just tell me, okay?

801
00:47:08,560 --> 00:47:11,720
But I think if I really want to meet Cent,

802
00:47:11,800 --> 00:47:14,160
it probably isn't beyond me.

803
00:47:15,280 --> 00:47:16,960
He and I will definitely meet.

804
00:47:18,800 --> 00:47:21,000
-Yuan, hold that spot for me.
-Okay.

805
00:47:21,080 --> 00:47:22,160
Hold still.

806
00:47:23,480 --> 00:47:26,760
Honestly, our pattern

807
00:47:26,840 --> 00:47:27,840
is freaking awesome.

808
00:47:29,080 --> 00:47:30,120
Yeah.

809
00:47:34,120 --> 00:47:35,640
Excuse me for a moment.

810
00:47:36,440 --> 00:47:37,400
Alright.

811
00:47:41,160 --> 00:47:42,720
What's up, madam?

812
00:47:42,800 --> 00:47:44,000
Are you free?

813
00:47:44,080 --> 00:47:46,680
I'm at Guy's condo.
We just finished checking the pattern.

814
00:47:49,280 --> 00:47:50,920
I'm here for work.

815
00:47:51,000 --> 00:47:53,240
Anyway, what's up?

816
00:47:53,920 --> 00:47:55,680
It's about Fuang's work.

817
00:47:56,200 --> 00:47:58,360
I'm worried about her.
She's been missing lately.

818
00:47:58,440 --> 00:48:02,120
After she's done helping Cent,
does she have any other jobs?

819
00:48:03,600 --> 00:48:05,640
Is she still doing character design?

820
00:48:07,000 --> 00:48:10,240
Does she have anywhere
to pitch her work soon? Do you know?

821
00:48:10,320 --> 00:48:12,920
If you mean pitching her work,
she's probably put that on hold.

822
00:48:13,560 --> 00:48:15,280
Cent came all the way
to her house to beg her.

823
00:48:15,360 --> 00:48:18,640
<i>He asked her back to help with the design.</i>

824
00:48:18,720 --> 00:48:20,080
<i>I was there when it happened.</i>

825
00:48:20,160 --> 00:48:23,000
But if I remember right,

826
00:48:23,080 --> 00:48:26,200
he asked her to get the brief
at his house tomorrow.

827
00:48:37,760 --> 00:48:42,360
POUND: PHOTO AND LOCATION
OF AUNT EIANG'S HOUSE

828
00:48:48,280 --> 00:48:50,120
Fuang didn't come to see Cent here?

829
00:48:51,560 --> 00:48:52,680
No, she didn't.

830
00:48:55,960 --> 00:48:56,800
Oh.

831
00:48:56,880 --> 00:48:59,720
I guess there must've been
a misunderstanding.

832
00:48:59,800 --> 00:49:01,440
I'm Franc, Fuang's friend.

833
00:49:01,520 --> 00:49:04,000
-Oh.
-She introduced me to Cent before.

834
00:49:04,080 --> 00:49:07,960
Today, she asked me to come here,
but she's not here at all.

835
00:49:08,760 --> 00:49:09,680
I'm confused too.

836
00:49:11,360 --> 00:49:14,480
Wait, maybe Fuang made an appointment
with Cent at his other house?

837
00:49:14,560 --> 00:49:17,680
His other house? Where is it?

838
00:49:17,760 --> 00:49:20,200
-Oh, it's at--
-Pong!

839
00:49:21,840 --> 00:49:24,680
Who are you talking to out front?
Why don't you come inside and talk?

840
00:49:24,760 --> 00:49:26,080
Are you Aunt Eiang?

841
00:49:26,640 --> 00:49:27,800
Hello.

842
00:49:27,880 --> 00:49:30,600
-I'm Franc, Fuang's friend.
-Mom!

843
00:49:31,200 --> 00:49:32,040
Auntie!

844
00:49:37,920 --> 00:49:39,920
Mom, get up.

845
00:49:46,360 --> 00:49:48,880
AUNT PED, JAI DEE CHILI PASTE

846
00:49:53,960 --> 00:49:57,280
PONG

847
00:49:57,360 --> 00:49:59,120
Oh no, Cent isn't picking up.

848
00:50:00,680 --> 00:50:03,600
I have a car.
Want me to drive her to the hospital?

849
00:50:03,680 --> 00:50:04,560
Thank you. Sorry to trouble you.

850
00:50:04,640 --> 00:50:05,760
-Sure. Let's go.
-No need.

851
00:50:05,840 --> 00:50:07,360
Auntie.

852
00:50:07,440 --> 00:50:09,160
It's okay. No need.

853
00:50:09,240 --> 00:50:12,960
I just felt faint.
I'll feel better after resting a bit.

854
00:50:14,960 --> 00:50:18,040
Are you sure, Auntie?
Please don't be polite.

855
00:50:18,120 --> 00:50:20,400
I checked on Google.
The hospital is only ten minutes away.

856
00:50:20,480 --> 00:50:22,960
Yes, I'm sure.

857
00:50:27,400 --> 00:50:28,680
What's your name again?

858
00:50:28,760 --> 00:50:30,200
My name is Franc.

859
00:50:30,280 --> 00:50:32,680
Franc is Fuang's friend.

860
00:50:33,440 --> 00:50:34,440
Franc.

861
00:50:36,560 --> 00:50:37,640
Fuang.

862
00:50:39,920 --> 00:50:41,480
Both are such cute names.

863
00:50:43,840 --> 00:50:45,720
What brings you here, dear?

864
00:50:49,320 --> 00:50:50,880
I came to see Fuang.

865
00:50:53,280 --> 00:50:55,000
Please give me two days.

866
00:50:55,080 --> 00:50:57,200
Once you approve it,
I'll make the prototype.

867
00:50:57,800 --> 00:50:58,760
Okay.

868
00:51:00,280 --> 00:51:02,640
That was quick. We got it done in no time.

869
00:51:05,400 --> 00:51:07,520
You're right. It only took a few minutes.

870
00:51:08,800 --> 00:51:10,440
Guess I'm explaining things better now.

871
00:51:11,680 --> 00:51:13,200
Or I'm getting faster at understanding.

872
00:51:13,280 --> 00:51:14,480
-Or both.
-Or both.

873
00:51:18,080 --> 00:51:19,320
Yes, both.

874
00:51:20,320 --> 00:51:21,800
I'll keep these documents.

875
00:51:21,880 --> 00:51:24,360
Okay. Then I'll get going.

876
00:51:40,200 --> 00:51:41,440
Cent.

877
00:51:42,280 --> 00:51:45,680
If I have another friend

878
00:51:45,760 --> 00:51:48,800
who wants to consult you,

879
00:51:49,680 --> 00:51:51,320
would you be available to talk to them?

880
00:51:51,920 --> 00:51:52,960
Who?

881
00:51:53,040 --> 00:51:56,360
In that case, I'll go look for Fuang now.

882
00:51:56,440 --> 00:51:58,240
Alright. Thank you so much.

883
00:51:58,880 --> 00:52:00,920
Then I'll take my leave.

884
00:52:01,000 --> 00:52:02,080
-Okay.
-Goodbye.

885
00:52:02,160 --> 00:52:04,360
-I'll walk you out.
-Pong, it's okay. You don't have to.

886
00:52:04,440 --> 00:52:05,720
Please stay and look after her.

887
00:52:05,800 --> 00:52:07,120
-Oh.
-Yes.

888
00:52:07,200 --> 00:52:09,120
-Goodbye.
-Alright. Take care.

889
00:52:19,120 --> 00:52:20,880
This friend of mine
is someone you know too.

890
00:52:21,520 --> 00:52:24,760
But I'll check with them to make sure.
Then I'll ask you again.

891
00:52:28,360 --> 00:52:30,880
Then I'll head home now.

892
00:52:33,840 --> 00:52:35,840
-Fuang.
-Yes?

893
00:52:37,600 --> 00:52:40,880
Manage your time well.
Don't forget to work on your own project.

894
00:52:43,360 --> 00:52:44,440
I won't forget.

895
00:52:45,760 --> 00:52:46,600
Bye.

896
00:53:29,760 --> 00:53:33,200
<i>If I have another friend</i>

897
00:53:33,280 --> 00:53:36,280
<i>who wants to consult you,</i>

898
00:53:37,200 --> 00:53:39,200
<i>would you be available to talk to them?</i>

899
00:53:44,920 --> 00:53:46,480
-Cent, I'm--
-Fuang told me.

900
00:53:50,200 --> 00:53:52,160
Come in. Close the gate too.

901
00:53:57,040 --> 00:53:58,440
I understand now

902
00:53:58,520 --> 00:54:00,680
that being an influencer
isn't easy at all.

903
00:54:00,760 --> 00:54:04,040
Honestly, I don't even know
what I'm supposed to do.

904
00:54:04,960 --> 00:54:07,640
Everything I think is good,
other people have already done it.

905
00:54:07,720 --> 00:54:09,480
Even my first YouTube episode

906
00:54:09,560 --> 00:54:12,720
is still a mess. I don't know
what to make or if anyone would watch.

907
00:54:12,800 --> 00:54:14,120
I'm still stressed about it.

908
00:54:14,200 --> 00:54:15,360
You came here to complain?

909
00:54:16,480 --> 00:54:19,480
If that's all, go home.
I don't have time to listen.

910
00:54:21,080 --> 00:54:23,840
I'm not complaining.
I'll get straight to the consultation.

911
00:54:23,920 --> 00:54:25,560
Go on. The problem is?

912
00:54:27,800 --> 00:54:29,440
What kind of content should I make?

913
00:54:29,520 --> 00:54:31,560
Asking that means you don't know yourself.

914
00:54:31,640 --> 00:54:33,360
You don't know what you're good at,

915
00:54:33,440 --> 00:54:36,200
you don't know what makes you interesting,

916
00:54:36,280 --> 00:54:38,640
and you don't even know
what you're interested in.

917
00:54:44,560 --> 00:54:48,120
Exactly. Then what should I do?

918
00:54:48,200 --> 00:54:50,360
Do I have to go find myself first?

919
00:54:50,440 --> 00:54:52,200
You think you'll find yourself
before you die?

920
00:54:52,280 --> 00:54:53,600
If all you do is find yourself,

921
00:54:54,240 --> 00:54:55,480
you'll never get anything done.

922
00:54:55,560 --> 00:54:57,560
Then how am I supposed to find the answer?

923
00:55:01,920 --> 00:55:04,640
What you need are, one, credibility.

924
00:55:04,720 --> 00:55:06,120
Two, people who believe in you.

925
00:55:06,200 --> 00:55:08,000
If you can't build those two things,

926
00:55:08,080 --> 00:55:10,400
you'll have no market value at all.

927
00:55:10,480 --> 00:55:12,800
Because you're not someone
coming in to generate income.

928
00:55:12,880 --> 00:55:15,040
You're someone coming in
looking for entertainment.

929
00:55:15,120 --> 00:55:17,880
You might make some money
while you're trending, but it won't last.

930
00:55:17,960 --> 00:55:19,480
That is not professional.

931
00:55:19,560 --> 00:55:22,960
As for the first episode's content,
it's inside you.

932
00:55:23,040 --> 00:55:26,240
Go find it yourself. I can't help you.

933
00:55:29,320 --> 00:55:31,640
<i>You need to find the group of people</i>
<i>who want to follow you.</i>

934
00:55:31,720 --> 00:55:34,600
<i>Find out what you're interested in</i>
<i>and what they're interested in too.</i>

935
00:55:34,680 --> 00:55:37,960
<i>Tell it the way you want to tell it</i>
<i>and the way they want to hear it.</i>

936
00:55:41,000 --> 00:55:42,720
When can you set up
a meeting with your dad for me?

937
00:55:43,480 --> 00:55:45,160
Why should I do that?

938
00:55:45,720 --> 00:55:48,080
You didn't pull off this deal.

939
00:55:48,160 --> 00:55:50,760
How did I not pull it off?
You got to talk to Cent, didn't you?

940
00:55:50,840 --> 00:55:52,320
You didn't do anything.

941
00:55:52,400 --> 00:55:55,080
You only told me
where his mom's house was.

942
00:55:55,160 --> 00:55:57,000
I handled the rest myself.

943
00:55:57,080 --> 00:55:59,360
But if I hadn't given you
Aunt Eiang's location,

944
00:55:59,440 --> 00:56:01,400
you still wouldn't have talked
to Cent by now.

945
00:56:01,480 --> 00:56:04,400
I got to talk to him
because I went in and handled it myself.

946
00:56:05,280 --> 00:56:07,280
Bottom line, you didn't
pull off this deal.

947
00:56:09,760 --> 00:56:12,640
That means you're not going
to set me up with your dad, right?

948
00:56:13,400 --> 00:56:14,840
No, that's not it.

949
00:56:15,440 --> 00:56:17,400
But you have to help me succeed first.

950
00:56:17,480 --> 00:56:21,120
Pull this off, and I'll set you up
with my dad. No conditions.

951
00:56:23,880 --> 00:56:24,840
What do you need help with?

952
00:56:30,440 --> 00:56:31,600
Take care of this too.

953
00:56:32,200 --> 00:56:33,800
-Hurry up, Pong.
-Yes.

954
00:56:37,000 --> 00:56:38,240
Are you okay, dear?

955
00:56:39,120 --> 00:56:41,920
Pound! What were you doing in my room?

956
00:56:42,000 --> 00:56:43,080
I don't want it.

957
00:56:46,960 --> 00:56:50,840
If you remember that I was the one
who introduced you to Cent,

958
00:56:51,680 --> 00:56:54,120
why didn't you tell me
you were going to see him?

959
00:56:54,200 --> 00:56:55,920
Let me introduce my friends first.

960
00:56:56,000 --> 00:56:58,080
This is Yuan, and this is Pound.

961
00:56:58,160 --> 00:57:00,240
And the busy ones
over there in the kitchen

962
00:57:00,320 --> 00:57:02,120
are Fuang and Bonus, those two brats.

963
00:57:03,240 --> 00:57:06,120
Those two brats? Seriously?

964
00:57:47,040 --> 00:57:52,040
Subtitle translation by:
Chomchanach Yanaharn
